{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '17,39p' tools/p10/qualification.py && sed -n '1630,1710p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/workbench_domain/send.rs && sed -n '255,335p' apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/adapters.rs && rg --files crates/desktop-core/tests | rg 'workbench|ui_v2_workbench' && python3 -c 'import json; r=json.load(open(\\\"docs/architecture/checks.json\\\")); print(json.dumps(r[\\\"chunks\\\"][\\\"C48\\\"],indent=2)); r=json.load(open(\\\"docs/architecture/native-checks.json\\\")); print(str(r)[-12500:])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '17,39p' tools/p10/qualification.py && sed -n '1630,1710p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/workbench_domain/send.rs && sed -n '255,335p' apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/adapters.rs && rg --files crates/desktop-core/tests | rg 'workbench|ui_v2_workbench' && python3 -c 'import json; r=json.load(open(\\\"docs/architecture/checks.json\\\")); print(json.dumps(r[\\\"chunks\\\"][\\\"C48\\\"],indent=2)); r=json.load(open(\\\"docs/architecture/native-checks.json\\\")); print(str(r)[-12500:])'\"","aggregated_output":"def read(path):\n    return json.loads(Path(path).read_text())\n\n\ndef sha(path):\n    return hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef digest(value):\n    return hashlib.sha256((json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\")) + \"\\n\").encode()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef bound(root, reference):\n    path = root / reference[\"path\"]\n    require(path.resolve().is_relative_to(root.resolve()), \"evidence escapes checkout\")\n    require(sha(path) == reference[\"sha256\"], \"evidence hash drift: \" + str(path))\n    return path\n\n\nEXACT_FIELDS = (\"executable_sha256\", \"bundle_sha256\", \"build_flags\", \"conditions\")\n\n\ndef verify_raw(root, needed, execution, origin):\n        Some(Err(r)) => return refusal(r),\n        Some(Ok(())) => {}\n    }\n    let Some(record) = find_run(inner, &scope, &run) else {\n        return refused(WorkbenchProblem::Missing);\n    };\n    let preview = if record.stored {\n        let keychain = Arc::clone(&inner.adapters.keychain);\n        let private = root.to_path_buf();\n        blocking(Vec::new(), move || {\n            history::preview(\n                &private,\n                keychain.as_ref(),\n                &scope,\n                &run,\n                history::PREVIEW_BYTES,\n            )\n            .unwrap_or_default()\n        })\n        .await\n    } else {\n        Vec::new()\n    };\n    WorkbenchResult::Ran {\n        run: run_view(record, &preview, false),\n    }\n}\n\n/// Saves a stored response body where the operator chooses.\npub(super) async fn save_response(inner: &Arc<Inner>, root: &Path, run: String) -> WorkbenchResult {\n    let scope = match open_scope(inner) {\n        Ok(s) => s,\n        Err(r) => return *r,\n    };\n    match load_history(inner, root, &scope, epoch(inner)).await {\n        None => return retired(),\n        Some(Err(r)) => return refusal(r),\n        Some(Ok(())) => {}\n    }\n    let Some(record) = find_run(inner, &scope, &run) else {\n        return refused(WorkbenchProblem::Missing);\n    };\n    if !record.stored {\n        return WorkbenchResult::SaveResponseFailed {\n            failure: ExportFailure::Body,\n        };\n    }\n    let name = record\n        .relative\n        .rsplit('/')\n        .next()\n        .unwrap_or(\"response\")\n        .trim_end_matches(\".request.toml\");\n    let name = name.split_whitespace().collect::<Vec<_>>().join(\"-\");\n    let json = record.headers.iter().any(|(n, v)| {\n        n.eq_ignore_ascii_case(\"content-type\") && v.to_ascii_lowercase().contains(\"json\")\n    });\n    let suggested = format!(\"{name}-response.{}\", if json { \"json\" } else { \"txt\" });\n    let Some(destination) = inner.adapters.folders.choose_save(suggested).await else {\n        return WorkbenchResult::Cancelled;\n    };\n    let name = destination\n        .file_name()\n        .map(|n| n.to_string_lossy().into_owned())\n        .unwrap_or_default();\n    let keychain = Arc::clone(&inner.adapters.keychain);\n    let private = root.to_path_buf();\n    let written = blocking(Err(ExportFailure::Io), move || {\n        history::export(&private, keychain.as_ref(), &scope, &run, &destination)\n    })\n    .await;\n    match written {\n        Ok(bytes) => WorkbenchResult::ResponseSaved { bytes, name },\n        Err(failure) => WorkbenchResult::SaveResponseFailed { failure },\n    }\n}\n\n/// Clears the open collection's history (not while one of its requests\n/// runs) and, separately, its cookies.\npub(super) async fn clear(inner: &Arc<Inner>, root: &Path, cookies: bool) -> WorkbenchResult {\n    let scope = match open_scope(inner) {\n    New,\n    /// The Harness's project folder (C21).\n    Project,\n    /// Save a response body under a suggested name (the panel confirms\n    /// replacing an existing file).\n    Save(String),\n}\n\nimpl<R: Runtime> NativeFolders<R> {\n    fn sheet(&self, sheet: Sheet) -> BoxFuture<'static, Option<PathBuf>> {\n        let app = self.app.clone();\n        Box::pin(async move {\n            let (tx, rx) = tokio::sync::oneshot::channel::<Option<PathBuf>>();\n            let window = app.get_webview_window(MAIN_WINDOW)?;\n            app.run_on_main_thread(move || {\n                let dialog = rfd::FileDialog::new().set_parent(&window);\n                let chosen = match sheet {\n                    Sheet::New => dialog\n                        .set_title(\"New collection\")\n                        .set_file_name(\"New collection\")\n                        .save_file(),\n                    Sheet::Open => dialog.set_title(\"Open collection\").pick_folder(),\n                    Sheet::Project => dialog.set_title(\"Choose project folder\").pick_folder(),\n                    Sheet::Save(name) => dialog\n                        .set_title(\"Save response\")\n                        .set_file_name(name)\n                        .save_file(),\n                };\n                let _ = tx.send(chosen);\n            })\n            .ok()?;\n            rx.await.ok()?\n        })\n    }\n}\n\nimpl<R: Runtime> FolderPicker for NativeFolders<R> {\n    fn choose_folder(&self) -> BoxFuture<'static, Option<PathBuf>> {\n        self.sheet(Sheet::Open)\n    }\n    fn choose_new(&self) -> BoxFuture<'static, Option<PathBuf>> {\n        self.sheet(Sheet::New)\n    }\n    fn choose_project(&self) -> BoxFuture<'static, Option<PathBuf>> {\n        self.sheet(Sheet::Project)\n    }\n    fn choose_save(&self, suggested: String) -> BoxFuture<'static, Option<PathBuf>> {\n        self.sheet(Sheet::Save(suggested))\n    }\n}\n\n/// Where the fixture driver stages Insomnia exports.\n#[cfg(feature = \"test-fixtures\")]\npub const FIXTURE_WORKBENCH_FILES: &str = \"fixture-workbench-files\";\n\n#[cfg(not(feature = \"test-fixtures\"))]\nfn workbench_files(_root: Option<&Path>) -> Arc<dyn ImportPicker> {\n    Arc::new(Cancelled)\n}\n\n/// Production builds use the native sheet (`sheet_picker` picks it).\n#[cfg(not(feature = \"test-fixtures\"))]\nstruct Cancelled;\n\n#[cfg(not(feature = \"test-fixtures\"))]\nimpl ImportPicker for Cancelled {\n    fn choose(&self) -> BoxFuture<'static, Option<Result<ImportFile, ImportError>>> {\n        Box::pin(async { None })\n    }\n}\n\n/// The fixture build answers the export sheet with the first file staged\n/// in `fixture-workbench-files/` (none: cancelled). The file is only read.\n#[cfg(feature = \"test-fixtures\")]\nfn workbench_files(root: Option<&Path>) -> Arc<dyn ImportPicker> {\n    struct Staged(Option<PathBuf>);\n    impl ImportPicker for Staged {\n        fn choose(&self) -> BoxFuture<'static, Option<Result<ImportFile, ImportError>>> {\n            let dir = self.0.clone();\n            Box::pin(async move {\n                let dir = dir?;\ncrates/desktop-core/tests/workbench_execution/main.rs\ncrates/desktop-core/tests/workbench_execution/server.rs\ncrates/desktop-core/tests/workbench_documents/main.rs\ncrates/desktop-core/tests/ui_v2_workbench/main.rs\n{\n  \"rust_target\": \"workbench_documents\",\n  \"check_commands\": [\n    [\n      \"cargo\",\n      \"fmt\",\n      \"--all\",\n      \"--\",\n      \"--check\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"cargo\",\n      \"run\",\n      \"--locked\",\n      \"-p\",\n      \"xtask\",\n      \"--\",\n      \"bindings\",\n      \"--check\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"pnpm\",\n      \"--filter\",\n      \"@prisma-airs/desktop-contracts\",\n      \"typecheck\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"pnpm\",\n      \"--filter\",\n      \"@prisma-airs/desktop\",\n      \"typecheck\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"cargo\",\n      \"check\",\n      \"--locked\",\n      \"-p\",\n      \"desktop-core\",\n      \"--lib\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"cargo\",\n      \"clippy\",\n      \"--locked\",\n      \"-p\",\n      \"desktop-core\",\n      \"--features\",\n      \"test-fixtures\",\n      \"--test\",\n      \"workbench_documents\",\n      \"--test\",\n      \"workbench_execution\",\n      \"--\",\n      \"-D\",\n      \"warnings\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"cargo\",\n      \"run\",\n      \"--locked\",\n      \"-p\",\n      \"xtask\",\n      \"--\",\n      \"notices\",\n      \"--check\"\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"fixture_command\": [\n    \"cargo\",\n    \"test\",\n    \"--locked\",\n    \"-p\",\n    \"desktop-core\",\n    \"--features\",\n    \"test-fixtures\",\n    \"--test\",\n    \"workbench_documents\",\n    \"refinement_startup_\"\n  ],\n  \"native_prepare\": [\n    \"cargo\",\n    \"run\",\n    \"--locked\",\n    \"-p\",\n    \"xtask\",\n    \"--\",\n    \"native-prepare\",\n    \"--chunk\",\n    \"C48\",\n    \"--target\",\n    \"aarch64-apple-darwin\",\n    \"--features\",\n    \"test-fixtures\"\n  ],\n  \"native_acceptance\": \"D063: C48 changed-flow assertions in native-checks.json on the current prepared candidate; preserve historical raw bindings and explicitly document unchanged-impact carry. No retired gate replay.\",\n  \"live_requirement\": \"fixtures only; any product diagnosis needs separately approved bounded live scope\",\n  \"host_commands\": [\n    [\n      \"cargo\",\n      \"test\",\n      \"--locked\",\n      \"-p\",\n      \"desktop-core\",\n      \"--features\",\n      \"test-fixtures\",\n      \"--test\",\n      \"workbench_execution\",\n      \"refinement_response_suggestions_\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"cargo\",\n      \"test\",\n      \"--locked\",\n      \"-p\",\n      \"desktop-core\",\n      \"--features\",\n      \"test-fixtures\",\n      \"--lib\",\n      \"workbench::profile::tests::an_existing_profile_has_an_uninitialized_collection_choice\"\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"frontend_commands\": [\n    [\n      \"pnpm\",\n      \"--filter\",\n      \"@prisma-airs/desktop\",\n      \"exec\",\n      \"vitest\",\n      \"run\",\n      \"--config\",\n      \"vitest.config.ts\",\n      \"src/v2/workbench/api-client.test.tsx\",\n      \"src/v2/workbench/request-presentation.test.ts\",\n      \"src/modules/workbench/document-save.test.tsx\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"pnpm\",\n      \"--filter\",\n      \"@prisma-airs/desktop\",\n      \"exec\",\n      \"vitest\",\n      \"run\",\n      \"--config\",\n      \"vitest.config.ts\",\n      \"src/v2/workbench/workbench.test.tsx\",\n      \"-t\",\n      \"announces request identity\"\n    ]\n  ]\n}\nnd exact under Raw; after the service changes a new send reflects it while History lists both runs and the older one shows exactly the first response; + creates a request draft (a new tab, 'New · not saved yet') and a Params row added in the table is written as a name=value line and shown by Preview; the Collection chip's menu opens Environments in a docked sheet, from the keyboard too (Space on the chip, Tab to Environments…, Space), and Escape or the sheet's close control returns focus to the Collection chip (I8, T09); nothing is sent by itself (D059 parity: the composites under evidence/C41/parity are captured by this script from the sent state, parity/bundle.json rewritten per capture, the owner's judgement recorded in parity/notes.md).\"}, {'id': 'C41-N02', 'check': \"Keyboard and layout (T09): from the URL field Tab reaches Send, Space sends and the completion is announced; the focus ring on Send; the API Client at 1440 wide by the display's working height and at 900×600 with 200% zoom, in light and dark, with the request open and sent, no horizontal page overflow, the tree, the request line and the response pane present with Send at least 32 CSS px; every row records the WebView's measured size and the viewport from its own tree and asserts them.\"}], 'C42': [{'id': 'C42-N01', 'check': \"The Academy as the prototype board draws it (R2App start=academy) around Academy's own learner pages with the Rust-owned theme: the title row (heading, lead, the account pill saying Browsing as a guest then the signed-in learner's name), the 1.4fr/1fr frame (the learner pages on the left with Academy's catalog heading and its trail; Your place on the right with the guest note and Open Settings, then signed in the sections Home · Learn · Program · Downloads · Notifications · Settings), the Learning paths row listing the synthetic catalog's paths as cards with their units and a card opening its path page; the guest generation reads the public catalog with no credential and the account generation after Sign in to Academy from Settings; the learner chrome stays inside the Academy region; the theme follows the appearance (light and dark captures) (D059 parity: the composites under evidence/C42/parity are captured by this script from the signed-in catalog state, parity/bundle.json rewritten per capture, the owner's judgement recorded in parity/notes.md).\"}, {'id': 'C42-N02', 'check': \"Keyboard and layout (T09): Tab from the first section link reaches the next section and a path card in order, the focus ring on a section link; the Academy at 1440 wide by the display's working height and at 900×600 with 200% zoom, in light and dark, signed in on the catalog, no horizontal page overflow, the frame's two cards and the Learning paths cards present with a path card at least 32 CSS px tall; every row records the WebView's measured size and the viewport from its own tree and asserts them.\"}], 'C43': [{'id': 'C43-N01', 'check': \"The first-run wizard as the prototype board draws it (R2Onboard, every step): the 320px rail with the brand tile, the numbered steps turning to checks as they are done, the Optional tags on Starter cases and Academy (Skipped once skipped), the privacy note and the appearance button; the pinned footer with Back, the hint, Step n of m, Skip for now and the primary; Welcome (tile, two paragraphs, three cards, no import box (D060)); Connect your tenant (the Tenant card's 2-column grid with the Environment segmented control and the Region select, Create tenant; then the scan key card tagged Required, the Management credentials card with Where do I find these?, the AI Gateway workspace card with its switch); Which products will you manage? (the 3-column product cards as checkboxes, Runtime always on, AIS and AES unavailable, the no-scan-key banner before a key is saved); Check the connection (the status banner, the Checks card with one row per line, Run the checks, Fix and verify again after a failure, Continue with warnings); Load starter test cases (the pack rows as checkboxes with counts, the summary, Skip for now); Join the AI Security Academy (Your account and What is sent cards, Skip for now); <name> is ready (the summary card with Change links, the three next-up cards, Open Prisma AIRS completing once) — the C29 behaviour unchanged (D059 parity: the composites under evidence/C43/parity are captured by this script per step, parity/bundle.json rewritten per capture, the owner's judgement recorded in parity/notes.md).\"}, {'id': 'C43-N02', 'check': \"The add-tenant sheet: a 1160×780 dialog without the modal's padding, the 244px rail (Tenant, Products, Verify, Starter cases, Done; no Welcome or Academy), Cancel in the footer on every step and no Back on the first; Cancel before a draft sends nothing; a drafted tenant's scan card is Optional and Continue is open; Cancel after a draft discards it in the core; Finish commits once and the sheet closes with the toast.\"}, {'id': 'C43-N03', 'check': \"Keyboard and layout (T09): Tab from the rail reaches the step's first field and the footer's primary in order; the focus ring on the primary; the wizard at 1440×900 and at 900×600 with 200% zoom, in light and dark, on the Tenant and Verify steps, no horizontal page overflow, the footer's primary inside the window and at least 32 CSS px; every row records the WebView's measured size and the viewport from its own tree and asserts them.\"}], 'C44': [{'id': 'C44-N01', 'check': \"One presentation (P09 closure): the fixture app's first run is the wizard with no Features rail and no 'Use the new interface' switch anywhere; after the tenant is set up, every destination the catalogue lists is opened from the Go menu (Home, Inbox, Harness, Academy, Test Cases, API Client, Administration; Runtime Security, AI Gateway and Red Team & Models opening Administration on their product; Sessions & Reports and Settings framed by the v2 shell (Import from v1 removed, D060)) under the v2 Destinations rail, each captured in light and dark at 1440×900 as the whole-app screenshot set under evidence/C44/parity/app, with no plaintext secret and no learner chrome (outside Academy) in any destination's tree; ⌘2 opens the Inbox and ⌘, Settings through the native menu; the built stylesheet carries the reduced-motion clamp; the bundle is Node-free and no Node, Bun or Deno process runs beside the app; after a quit and relaunch 15 s of startup open no internet socket from the app or its WebKit processes, Home shows with the tenant active and Administration reads with the kept client; every pre-P09 native assertion has its standing in evidence/C44/legacy-script-map.md (exercised by a named v2 check, self-run through legacy_v2 — C03, C04, C05, C06, C07, C10, C11, C24 — ported into this check, or retired with its reason) and the mapped drivers' records on this bundle bind the gate: an exercised, self-run or ported assertion without a passing target fails this check.\"}], 'C45': [{'id': 'C45-N01', 'check': 'Prepared real fixture is Prisma AIRS Desktop Fixture1.0.0, identifierio.cdot.airs-desktop.fixture, binaryprisma-airs-desktop. Production config independently names Prisma AIRS Desktop1.0.0/io.cdot.airs-desktop. Native About/menu/title and Home-first catalogue agree; startup/settings/sessions focus and headings use the one presentation. Exact candidate process identity, executable and complete bundle are bound.'}, {'id': 'C45-N02', 'check': 'Fresh synthetic setup starts with the wizard and no adopted tenants, credentials, sessions or approvals. Controlled prior alpha/v2 root/service canaries remain byte-identical across setup/relaunch/reset. Old real application roots, login Keychain and live endpoints are never inspected. Namespace isolation and non-adoption require passing production-interface FileStore/authority and disposable-file Keychain regressions, not only absence of UI.'}, {'id': 'C45-N03', 'check': 'No alternate presentation selector or alpha/tenant-profile/API-profile-adoption surface or native intent remains. Ordinary current-format collection open/create/import/editor behavior is retained, along with active Settings/Sessions/Diagnostics/Academy behavior and C44 scope/commit-phase guards. Every current mapped legacy/modern target is accounted by the same candidate baseline or explicit valid coverage proof; no assertion disappears via omission.'}], 'C46': [{'id': 'C46-N01', 'check': 'New first-run and Add/replacement tenant require actual successful management OAuth before commitment. Invalid/missing OAuth cannot complete, product-forbidden OAuth success stays a separate warning, Scan Key can be added later without a validation scan. Cancel leaves prior active tenant and draft credential cleanup intact; bound production-interface regressions establish stale/retry/persistence cases.'}, {'id': 'C46-N02', 'check': 'Dedicated setup recheck shows precise failing Supply Chain source or Gateway prerequisite, stays active for failed/unknown/different scope, clears only a matching fresh pass and retains original reason/date in Diagnostics. Ordinary Refresh does not clear the finding. Gateway checks listed slug in IAM, not displayed UUID; synthetic fixtures only.'}, {'id': 'C46-N03', 'check': 'Model/Skill Inbox action opens Administration on AI Supply Chain Security through the complete product arrival path; Runtime resource filters still arrive correctly. Original dated diagnostics and latest recheck provenance are readable; navigation never grants remote write authority.'}], 'C47': [{'id': 'C47-N01', 'check': 'One focusable app-header H1 names the destination; content starts with concise bounded description beside actions. Home, Inbox, Test Cases, API Client, Administration, Settings, Harness and Academy remain usable at ordinary and narrow effective widths/200% zoom. Academy course/unit hierarchy remains intact.'}, {'id': 'C47-N02', 'check': 'Explain overlays the right without changing page width. Page controls and navigation remain usable; drawer scroll/Close/Escape/focus work, modal priority is preserved, and tenant switch closes/retire previous selection including pending-open race.'}, {'id': 'C47-N03', 'check': 'Redundant header Ask Harness is absent while sidebar navigation remains. Improved sun glyph, existing light/dark action label and checked state are visible and agree with the actual toggle action; keyboard and focus states remain readable in light/dark.'}], 'C48': [{'id': 'C48-N01', 'check': 'Editable request JSON and complete URL show colored tokens once while native input owns text/cursor/selection/IME/copy. Pretty JSON colors exact large-integer/escape tokens; invalid/truncated preview degrades safely. Raw/copy/saved bytes remain exact; Save is admitted exactly once.'}, {'id': 'C48-N02', 'check': 'Request tabs occupy one horizontally scrolling row and reveal selected/focused tabs. Bottom Ready/request-count status shows only displayed request/run/history metrics; late/background/old-collection replies cannot overwrite it. Active Cancel and separate save state remain usable.'}, {'id': 'C48-N03', 'check': 'First use loads SCM193; chosen built-in/custom or explicitly closed state survives restart. Missing/replaced/redirected custom root offers recovery without fallback or folder creation. Native Save Response suggests hyphenated whitespace-normalized basename and respects explicitly chosen filename/directory, preserving bytes.'}], 'C49': [{'id': 'C49-N01', 'check': 'Settings uses compact Appearance, Academy and Diagnostics cards, with a dedicated Tenant section containing Scan Key, Management Client, Scan Destination, Update Tenant and Add Tenant cards. Controls remain keyboard-accessible and usable at narrow width/200% zoom.'}, {'id': 'C49-N02', 'check': 'Independent Appearance and Theme dropdowns provide Prisma AIRS default and Gruvbox light/dark. Existing Appearance survives restart; alternate theme persists. Representative shell/product, learner and portaled surfaces retain contrast/focus and Academy-owned cosmetics; desktop theme grants no earned skin.'}, {'id': 'C49-N03', 'check': 'Credential cards preserve secure/session choices and Replace/Remove; secrets clear before async work and context changes. Add uses isolated required-OAuth draft. Edit changes only selected label/environment without identity/credential rebind; Delete stays target-bound; custom HTTPS destination remains in its reviewed card. Production-interface rollback/isolation regressions are bound alongside native interaction.'}]}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
